WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:07.070
In House of the Dragon Episode 3, the king
kills a stag, the princess kills a boar, and

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.480
the prince kills a crab.. feeder.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.820
There’s a battle, and a party, and no one
has fun except for this pug.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.039
So what happens, and what does it mean?

00:00:17.039 --> 00:00:21.150
This video has no spoilers beyond Hot D Episode
3.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.300
The episode starts about three years after
the previous episode.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.160
King Viserys has married Alicent Hightower,
they’ve had a baby named Aegon, and and

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.880
Alicent is pregnant with another child.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.270
To celebrate Aegon’s second birthday, they
hold a royal hunt.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.910
We saw a royal hunt in the original Game of
Thrones show – and Thrones author George

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:46.320
Martin said this was his “least favorite
scene in the entire show”.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.090
Because this hunt is just four dudes walking
in the woods.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:57.320
George said a royal hunt should be a big event
with a hundred dudes, and tents and dogs and

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.320
horns.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.760
So the hunt in Hot D is much closer to the
author’s vision – with tents and dogs

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.360
and horns.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:10.250
They hunt in the kingswood, which is a forest
near King’s Landing where only the king

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.570
is allowed to hunt animals.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:19.020
Last episode mentioned a poacher who was “brought
to justice” for the crime of hunting here.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:23.470
So the hunt is like a big festival, with lots
of food and guests.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:28.220
Viserys wants everyone to just have fun and
celebrate.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.730
But the lords have political agendas.

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:38.100
Hobert Hightower is the Lord of Oldtown, and
he’s the older brother of Otto Hightower,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.590
the Hand of the King.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:45.060
The Hightowers want King Viserys to make Alicent
Hightower’s son Aegon heir to the Throne

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.979
– instead of Rhaenyra, who Viserys earlier
named as heir.

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:55.640
Cause if Otto’s grandson becomes king, that
could make the Hightowers more powerful.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.890
Previously, it seemed like Otto was motivated
by his own ambition.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:05.050
But now we see Hobert pressuring him and telling
him what to do.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:10.429
Last episode, Corlys talked about “second
sons”, how younger brothers are overshadowed

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:14.420
by their older brother, and have to fight
for a place in the world.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:20.600
We see that dynamic in Hobert and Otto, and
in Corlys and Vaemond, and in Viserys and

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:24.230
Daemon – lots of brother stuff this episode.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:28.820
We meet Jason Lannister, and his twin brother
Tyland Lannister.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:33.349
These guys are ancestors of Cersei, Jaime
and Tyrion Lannister.

00:02:33.349 --> 00:02:36.150
Jason is the Lord of Casterly Rock.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:41.490
And Tyland is now on Viserys’ council as
master of ships, to replace Corlys.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:45.709
The books say that Viserys chose Tyland to
be master of ships because the Lannisters

00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:49.390
supported Viserys back at the Harrenhal council.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:54.810
Jason and Tyland are both played by actor
Jefferson Hall – who once played Ser Hugh

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.700
in Game of Thrones Season 1.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.380
&gt;You might not remember Hugh cause he didn’t
last very long.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.640
Lord Lyonel Strong brings his sons, Larys
and Harwin.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:11.200
Harwin is said to be the strongest knight
in the realm, and has the nickname “Breakbones”.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:17.150
Larys is called the Clubfoot, because he has
a deformed foot, and has trouble walking.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:23.040
So instead of joining the hunt, he sits with
the ladies, and listens quietly.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.170
The official website says Larys is “ingenious”
but “underestimated”.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:35.239
The name Larys sounds like Varys, and Varys
is also a man who listens, and knows the value

00:03:35.239 --> 00:03:37.590
of information.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:43.660
Princess Rhaenyra reads in the godswood, making
a minstrel play the same song over and over

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.610
like an iPod on repeat.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:50.490
The minstrel’s name is Samwell, which might
be a reference to Casablanca, when a musician

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:53.280
called Sam has to keep playing the same song.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:59.490
Rhaenyra’s song, and Rhaenyra’s book,
are about Nymeria, the ancient eastern princess

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:03.260
who sailed across the sea to escape the dragonlords.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:07.500
Like Nymeria, Rhaenyra dreams of freedom and
escape.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.040
In Episode 1, we saw Rhaenyra and Alicent
here when they were best friends.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:18.209
But now Rhaenyra is cold and distant to Alicent
– she still feels angry and betrayed that

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:23.080
her friend suddenly became her step-mum and
her queen.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:28.180
Rhaenyra tells the minstrel to stay, but Alicent
tells him to leave – and the minstrel obeys

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:35.220
Alicent, not Rhaenyra – cause Queen Alicent
now outranks Princess Rhaenyra.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:41.050
Rhaenyra hates that she’s been replaced
by Alicent, so she refuses Alicent’s attempts

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.620
to reconnect.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:47.819
On the road, Alicent says that her baby’s
birth was quick and easy – and then there’s

00:04:47.819 --> 00:04:53.749
an awkward pause, cause everyone’s reminded
of Rhaenyra’ mum Aemma, who died in childbirth

00:04:53.749 --> 00:04:55.509
in Episode 1.

00:04:55.509 --> 00:04:58.759
At the hunting camp, everyone cheers for baby
Aegon.

00:04:58.759 --> 00:05:04.169
Aegon’s granduncle, Hobert Hightower, calls
Aegon “Second of His Name”, and “His

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:09.839
Grace”, which is what you would say if Aegon
was king – even though officially Rhaenyra

00:05:09.839 --> 00:05:11.580
is heir to the Throne.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.279
Many lords want a male ruler, not a woman.

00:05:15.279 --> 00:05:20.580
So while everyone cheers Aegon, Rhaenyra sits
alone and ignored.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:24.949
We hear that Lady Johanna Swann was abducted
in the Stepstones.

00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:32.190
Cause the Stepstones are occupied by the Triarchy,
the eastern alliance led by the Crabfeeder.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:37.490
The books say that the Triarchy impose heavy
taxes on ships passing through the Stepstones

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:38.869
trade routes.

00:05:38.869 --> 00:05:41.310
And they don’t just take money.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:46.909
The Triarchy kidnap people and sell them into
sex slavery in the city of Lys.

00:05:46.909 --> 00:05:52.199
Johanna Swann was the fifteen year old niece
of a lord, and after being kidnapped she became

00:05:52.199 --> 00:05:57.649
a famous courtesan in Lys, and eventually
was the ruler of the city, “known as the

00:05:57.649 --> 00:05:59.210
Black Swan”.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:03.649
We meet Ceira Lannister, the mother of Jason
and Tyland.

00:06:03.649 --> 00:06:08.939
And we meet Lady Joselyn of House Redwyne
– an ancestor of the Queen of Thorns.

00:06:08.939 --> 00:06:13.599
Joselyn criticises King Viserys, so Rhaenyra
insults Joselyn.

00:06:13.599 --> 00:06:17.580
It’s funny, but it’s probably not smart.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:23.280
If Rhaenyra wants to rule, she needs allies,
and insulting powerful people is not gonna

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:24.280
help.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:29.050
Despite being heir to the Throne, Rhaenyra
isn’t acting like a politician – she’s

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:31.479
more like a grumpy teenager.

00:06:31.479 --> 00:06:36.819
While Alicent acts more diplomatically – she
behaves like a queen.

00:06:36.819 --> 00:06:42.240
Jason Lannister tries to flirt with Rhaenyra
– cause Rhaenyra is now of an age to be

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:46.009
married, and as a royal princess, everyone
wants her.

00:06:46.009 --> 00:06:50.939
Jason tries to impress Rhaenyra by bragging
about his wealth – the Lannisters are the

00:06:50.939 --> 00:06:55.279
second richest family in the realm, after
the Velaryons.

00:06:55.279 --> 00:06:57.710
Jason says that he’s got a really big penis.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:03.740
I mean a really big castle – Casterly Rock
is taller than the Hightower and taller than

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:04.740
the Wall.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:10.249
In the books, it’s a mountain with tunnels
and rooms carved into it – though when we

00:07:10.249 --> 00:07:15.030
saw Casterly Rock in Game of Thrones it was..
not as impressive.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:20.559
Jason says that he could build a Dragonpit,
so if Rhaenyra marries him she could keep

00:07:20.559 --> 00:07:22.979
dragons at Casterly Rock.

00:07:22.979 --> 00:07:27.379
This is not the first time Lannisters have
tried to get dragons.

00:07:27.379 --> 00:07:30.780
The old king Jaehaerys, had a sister called
Rhaena.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:34.889
Rhaena and her dragon Dreamfyre stayed with
the Lannisters for a while.

00:07:34.889 --> 00:07:39.869
And the Lannisters tried to convince Rhaena
to give the Lannisters dragon eggs, or to

00:07:39.869 --> 00:07:43.939
marry a Lannister so that their children could
have Targaryen dragon blood.

00:07:43.939 --> 00:07:48.979
Cause “With dragonriders of their own, the
Lannisters” could be as powerful as the

00:07:48.979 --> 00:07:50.309
Targaryens.

00:07:50.309 --> 00:07:54.530
Many of the great houses were kings before
the Targaryens took over.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:08:00.129
So all the proud lords are envious of Targaryen
dragon power.

00:08:00.129 --> 00:08:03.370
Rhaenyra is angry that Viserys wants to marry
her off.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:07.759
She doesn’t want to be sent away to live
with some husband, and she doesn’t want

00:08:07.759 --> 00:08:11.449
Viserys to disinherit her and give the Throne
to Aegon instead.

00:08:11.449 --> 00:08:17.249
Viserys handles his unhappy daughter by shouting
at her at a public political event, which

00:08:17.249 --> 00:08:18.471
is a terrible idea.

00:08:18.471 --> 00:08:24.409
And Rhaenyra rides away, like Princess Nymeria
fleeing the dragonlords.

00:08:24.409 --> 00:08:31.169
Otto says there’s been a sighting of a white
hart, a deer with a rare pale colour.

00:08:31.169 --> 00:08:37.180
In Westeros, and in real mythology, a white
hart is seen as a rare blessing from the gods,

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.050
and a symbol of royalty.

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:44.820
If they catch this white hart on baby Aegon’s
birthday, it could be seen as a sign that

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:47.950
Aegon should be the heir to the Throne.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:53.370
Otto admits that he doesn’t normally believe
in “signs and portents” – but he will

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:58.630
pretend to believe any old crap if it means
his grandson becomes king.

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:03.190
Jason Lannister gives Viserys a fancy spear
to honour Aegon.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:07.570
Gifts are a way to try to win political favours
from kings.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:12.870
Jason mentions the Golden Gallery, which is
a place in Casterly Rock with “gilded ornaments

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:17.730
and walls”, it sounds like the Palace of
Versailles or someplace.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:23.200
Jason says he expects Aegon to become heir
instead of Rhaenyra, so Viserys drunkenly

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:27.690
shit talks and teases the Lannister to put
him in his place.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:33.030
Like how King Robert made fun of Lancel Lannister
in Game of Thrones.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:39.760
King Robert and King Viserys are both charismatic
characters who suck at being king and use

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:45.190
alcohol to cope while terrible conflicts rise
up around them.

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:49.820
Otto tells Viserys that he should marry Rhaenyra
to Aegon.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:57.070
Viserys laughs at the absurdity of marrying
his daughter to her two-year-old half-brother.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:02.300
But the age gap between Rhaenyra and Aegon
is less than the gap between Viserys and his

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.790
wife Alicent.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:09.050
And the Targaryens have a long tradition of
marrying their siblings – Viserys’ parents

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:12.040
were siblings, and his grandparents were siblings.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:17.980
So since Rhaenyra and Aegon are only half-siblings,
&lt;this would be one of the less incestuous

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:20.580
Targaryen royal marriages.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:25.370
Marrying a Targaryen would prevent other families
from potentially getting dragons.

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:29.950
And a Rhaenyra-Aegon marriage could prevent
any potential conflict between the two for

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:31.180
the Throne.

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:36.900
But Viserys is sick of the “fucking politicking”,
and returns to his wine.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:41.670
The king is surrounded by people, but is very
alone and stressed.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:48.060
Viserys is now missing two fingers – his
finger was cut on the Throne in Episode 1,

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:53.480
and was rotting in Episode 2 – now the infected
fingers have been amputated.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:11:00.350
The king is literally falling apart, disintegrating
under the weight of his crown.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:07.280
Lord Lyonel Strong says Viserys is not first
Targaryen king to have trouble with his daughter.

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:13.240
The previous king Jaehaerys had constant problems
with his daughters – Alyssa was a wild tomboy,

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:19.290
Daella was a scaredy-cat, Saera ran off to
a brothel, Viserra was a narcissist.

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:23.420
Lyonel says rebellious Targaryen girls are
“tradition”.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:28.600
Of course, if every generation of Targaryen
women struggles against the political system,

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:33.020
that might be a sign that it’s the system
that’s the problem, not the women.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:37.850
They discuss a husband for Rhaenyra, and Viserys
expects Lyonel to say that Rhaenyra should

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:39.980
marry his son Harwin.

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:45.910
But turns out Lyonel is the one guy who doesn’t
recommend his own family’s interests.

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:49.630
Lyonel says Rhaenyra should marry Laenor Velaryon.

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:56.780
Laenor is the son of Corlys Velaryon and Rhaenys
Targaryen – heir to the rich House Velaryon.

00:11:56.780 --> 00:12:01.620
Marrying Laenor could finally fix the tension
between the Targaryens and Velaryons – after

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:06.750
Viserys rejected Laena Velaryon, and Rhaenys
was rejected at the Harrenhal Council.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:13.680
Viserys seems to appreciate that Lyonel gives
unbiased advice, but he also is too wasted

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:16.040
to walk in a straight line.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:22.240
So Rhaenyra runs off to the woods, and she’s
followed by her sworn protector, Criston Cole.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:26.260
Rhaenyra and Criston have become close over
the last few years.

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:31.780
Rhaenyra complains about being married off,
about not having a choice, and being powerless.

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:37.170
But Criston reminds her she’s a princess
and her life is way better than most peoples

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.560
lives in this medieval world.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:45.250
And Rhaenyra is not powerless – by choosing
Criston for the Kingsguard, Rhaenyra changed

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.420
Criston’s life for the better.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:52.980
As a lower class person, Criston can give
Rhaenyra the perspective of someone less privileged

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:54.710
than her.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:58.540
Rhaenyra insists on hanging in the woods instead
of returning to camp.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.960
And they get attacked by a boar.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:06.420
Criston wounds the animal, and then Rhaenyra
brutally stabs it to death, unleashing her

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:09.120
emotions through violence.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:14.210
Rhaenyra is full of suppressed anger at her
father, and pain from Alicent’s betrayal,

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:18.160
and she lets it all out on this animal.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:24.140
Rhaenyra said earlier that dying boars squeal
like children – and then the child Aegon

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:25.970
made a sound.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:32.640
So now when Rhaenyra kills this squealing
boar, maybe she imagines stabbing Aegon, the

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:35.820
baby that threatens to replace her as heir.

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:39.850
Viserys tells Alicent about his dreams.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:42.910
Many Targaryens have prophetic dreams of the
future.

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:48.130
Like, Daenys Targaryen dreamed about the Doom
of Valyria before it happened – that’s

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:51.480
how the Targaryens escaped the Doom and came
to Westeros.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:57.420
Daenys wrote a book of her visions called
Signs and Portents – which is the same phrase

00:13:57.420 --> 00:14:00.500
Otto uses to describe the white hart.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:05.320
We know that Viserys once dreamed that he
would have a son and that son would king.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:10.660
But when Aemma and her son died, Viserys lost
faith in this dream.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:15.950
He gave up on having a son, and so he named
Rhaenyra his heir.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:22.230
But now that Viserys finally has a son, Aegon,
he’s doubting himself again.

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:28.160
Maybe his dream of a son was right after all,
and Aegon should be the heir, not Rhaenyra.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:33.810
The white hart is part of his doubt – if
they find the white hart on Aegon’s birthday,

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:37.970
that sign might convince Viserys that Aegon
should be heir.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:44.400
So Viserys is full of doubt and guilt and
grief, which is similar to other Targaryen

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.580
dreamers.

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:51.490
In The Hedge Knight prequel story, Daeron
Targaryen feels tortured by his dreams, and

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:55.830
uses alcohol to try to escape them to a dreamless
sleep.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:15:02.360
Daeron’s brother Aemon says dreams killed
his brothers, every one.

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:08.470
Alicent looks concerned that her husband and
king is drunkenly rambling about using dreams

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:12.620
to decide the future of the realm and of her
son.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:17.700
In the morning, they find a deer, but it’s
not the white hart – it’s just a normal

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:18.940
brown deer.

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:24.260
So Viserys feels relieved – there was no
special omen on Aegon’s birthday, so maybe

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:28.580
Viserys made the right choice after all and
Rhaenyra should be the heir.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:34.790
Viserys is expected to kill this deer, even
though he didn’t hunt it down, and he doesn’t

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:36.860
really want to kill it.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:43.340
This is similar to how Viserys had his wife
Aemma killed – she also was held down and

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:46.980
helpless, sacrificed reluctantly by Viserys.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:53.240
It’s the job of a king to sacrifice people
for the good of the realm – soldiers in

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.279
battle, women in childbirth.

00:15:55.279 --> 00:16:00.330
But Viserys’ compassion makes him reluctant
to make these hard decisions, and that’s

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:02.880
why it’s hard for him to be king.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:07.830
Viserys fails to kill the deer cleanly, and
has to stab it twice.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:09.800
Which is another bad omen.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:16.279
It’s like when Theon struggles to kill Rodrik
in Game of Thrones – this violence is ugly

00:16:16.279 --> 00:16:20.100
and cold and farcical and makes everybody
look bad.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:27.110
The deer can represent King Viserys himself
– cause the deer is a strong regal animal,

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:32.550
but it’s also constrained, struggling, pulled
in different directions by these men, just

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:37.400
as Viserys is pulled in different directions
by his lords and their politics.

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:44.029
In Game of Thrones Episode 1, a dead stag
foreshadows the death of King Robert, killed

00:16:44.029 --> 00:16:49.430
by a boar – so this dead stag could be foreshadowing
for Viserys.

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:53.910
Meanwhile, Rhaenyra is covered in the blood
of her violence.

00:16:53.910 --> 00:17:00.610
Her killing was not some fake ceremonial slaughter,
it was real hot-blooded violence to defend

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:02.510
herself from attack.

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:07.369
And as she looks over the kingswood, the white
hart appears to her.

00:17:07.369 --> 00:17:12.939
Just walks right up like some mystical sign
from the gods that Rhaenyra should be the

00:17:12.939 --> 00:17:13.939
heir.

00:17:13.939 --> 00:17:18.649
Criston draws his sword, but Rhaenyra tells
him not to kill the hart.

00:17:18.649 --> 00:17:24.169
This shows that Rhaenyra can be merciful and
peaceful, in contrast to her killing of the

00:17:24.169 --> 00:17:25.289
boar.

00:17:25.289 --> 00:17:29.169
Not killing the white hart also fits with
the animal’s mythology.

00:17:29.169 --> 00:17:34.330
In the Game of Thrones books, Sansa thinks
that in the stories, knights never harm white

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:35.510
harts.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:39.899
So Rhaenyra plays the role of the gentle heroes
in the stories.

00:17:39.899 --> 00:17:45.909
But if Rhaenyra did kill the white hart and
showed everyone back at camp, that might’ve

00:17:45.909 --> 00:17:47.990
convinced people to support her as heir.

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:53.760
Her choice not to kill the hart might represent
Rhaenyra choosing not to go for the Throne.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:18:00.039
So just like the dreams and prophecies, this
mystical sign is ambiguous – it’s up to

00:18:00.039 --> 00:18:05.279
the characters and the viewers to decide what
this sign means.

00:18:05.279 --> 00:18:09.750
Rhaenyra brings the boar back to camp, so
she still gets to prove herself to everyone.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:16.100
Jason Lannister is grossed out, but Harwin
Strong is visibly into it.

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:19.090
Back at the Red Keep, Otto speaks with his
daughter Alicent.

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:24.720
They’re quite formal and distant with each
other – Otto calls Alicent “Your Grace”,

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:30.850
which suggests that Otto sees Alicent more
as a political asset than as his daughter.

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:35.990
Otto says that her son Aegon will inherit
the Throne, because he’s male,.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:41.639
Alicent says Rhaenyra is the heir, but Otto
tells her to convince Viserys to name Aegon

00:18:41.639 --> 00:18:43.570
heir.

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:48.639
Alicent speaks with Viserys, and tells him
that Rhaenyra will marry if she thinks it’s

00:18:48.639 --> 00:18:54.350
her choice to marry – which sounds a bit
manipulative, but it also shows that Alicent

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:58.850
understands Rhaenyra’s feelings and wants
her to be happy.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:02.299
Alicent learns that the war in the Stepstones
is going badly.

00:19:02.299 --> 00:19:07.190
Viserys doesn’t want to help Daemon and
Corlys, because Daemon and Corlys started

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:11.740
this war against Viserys’ wishes – he
doesn’t want to look weak.

00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:17.130
But Alicent says Viserys should do what’s
best for the realm, regardless of his personal

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:18.130
feelings.

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:19.879
Which is what a king should do.

00:19:19.879 --> 00:19:24.649
And Alicent doesn’t bring up making Aegon
heir like Otto told her to – so Alicent

00:19:24.649 --> 00:19:29.649
doesn’t just go along with her father’s
plots, she advocates for the greater good

00:19:29.649 --> 00:19:33.230
instead – maybe Alicent is a good queen.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:37.500
This is the first episode where we don’t
see Alicent picking at her fingernails.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:40.149
She has become more confident.

00:19:40.149 --> 00:19:44.129
But her exact goals and plans are not yet
clear.

00:19:44.129 --> 00:19:49.669
Viserys listens to Alicent, and sends reinforcements
to help Daemon and the Velaryons.

00:19:49.669 --> 00:19:53.600
Viserys and Rhaenyra argue some more about
Rhaenyra getting married.

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:59.950
Viserys admits that he married Alicent out
of selfish desire, not political advantage.

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:03.499
So he says he’ll let Rhaenyra choose who
she wants to marry.

00:20:03.499 --> 00:20:08.470
And Viserys swears that he won’t replace
Rhaenyra as heir.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:14.639
So Viserys affirms his support for Rhaenyra..
privately, but many of the lords still see

00:20:14.639 --> 00:20:16.509
Aegon as heir.

00:20:16.509 --> 00:20:21.470
And if Rhaenyra marries for desire instead
of for political advantage, she might not

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:26.539
have the support she needs to claim the Throne
when Viserys dies.

00:20:26.539 --> 00:20:32.649
While the royalty are plotting and feasting,
on the Stepstones, men are fighting for their

00:20:32.649 --> 00:20:33.649
lives.

00:20:33.649 --> 00:20:38.539
The Velaryons and Prince Daemon are at war
against the Triarchy, led by the Crabfeeder.

00:20:38.539 --> 00:20:42.100
And the war is going badly for the Westerosi.

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:46.739
We see Daemon attacking the Triarchy with
his dragon Caraxes, but the Triarchy learn

00:20:46.739 --> 00:20:50.299
to avoid the dragons by hiding in caves.

00:20:50.299 --> 00:20:55.330
These guerrilla tactics are similar to how
the Dornish successfully resisted Aegon’s

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:56.330
Conquest.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:21:01.499
We see Daemon’s dragon stomp on one of his
own men, which shows that Daemon doesn’t

00:21:01.499 --> 00:21:03.860
really care who he kills.

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:07.649
And shows that dragons are not precise weapons.

00:21:07.649 --> 00:21:13.419
When dragons go to war, there’s collateral
damage, and ordinary people get killed.

00:21:13.419 --> 00:21:19.539
Daemon gets shot with an arrow, and his dragon
Caraxes cries out as though in pain.

00:21:19.539 --> 00:21:25.309
The books say there’s a mysterious bond
between dragon and dragonrider, like some

00:21:25.309 --> 00:21:30.360
psychic connection that lets dragons feel
what their riders feel.

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:34.429
The Starks and their direwolves have a similar
connection in the books.

00:21:34.429 --> 00:21:40.070
So Daemon and Caraxes cause some havok, but
they fail to find the Crabfeeder.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:43.590
The Velaryons are led by Lord Corlys Velaryon.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:49.549
We also meet Corlys’ younger brother Vaemond
Velaryon, a commander in their navy.

00:21:49.549 --> 00:21:55.309
Vaemond seems to have a combative relationship
with his brother – like Viserys and Daemon,

00:21:55.309 --> 00:21:56.669
and Hobert and Otto.

00:21:56.669 --> 00:22:00.489
Laenor Velaryon is the son of Corlys and Rhaenys.

00:22:00.489 --> 00:22:05.470
He seems to have had a big growth spurt since
we saw him in Episode 1.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:07.669
And this guy is Ser Joffrey Lonmouth.

00:22:07.669 --> 00:22:13.039
He’s called the Knight of Kisses, because
the heraldry of House Lonmouth has red lips

00:22:13.039 --> 00:22:14.039
and skulls.

00:22:14.039 --> 00:22:19.159
The Velaryons are outnumbered, they’re running
out of food, they fear they’ll be eaten

00:22:19.159 --> 00:22:20.409
by the crabs.

00:22:20.409 --> 00:22:25.280
But then Daemon finds out that his brother
Viserys sent reinforcements to help them – which

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:27.879
you’d think would be good news.

00:22:27.879 --> 00:22:31.789
But Daemon gets so angry that he beats up
the messenger.

00:22:31.789 --> 00:22:37.730
Cause as Viserys said, Daemon would rather
die than accept help from his big brother.

00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:43.760
Daemon is here to prove himself, to show that
he can win by his own strength.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:51.059
So before Viserys’ reinforcements arrive,
Daemon leads a suicidally dangerous attack.

00:22:51.059 --> 00:22:55.980
The plan is for Daemon to lure the Crabfeeder
from his caves.

00:22:55.980 --> 00:23:02.250
So Daemon goes alone, and he pretends to surrender,
by waving a white flag.

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:05.570
Only to betray the Triarchy and attack them
anyway.

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:10.559
It’s like in Game of Thrones when Ramsay
gets Theon to use a peace banner to get some

00:23:10.559 --> 00:23:16.440
ironborn to surrender, but Ramsay betrays
the ironborn and kills them anyway.

00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:21.419
This is another example of Daemon breaking
rules to get what he wants.

00:23:21.419 --> 00:23:28.149
Daemon single-handedy kills like a dozen dudes,
dodges arrows, does a barrel roll, and somehow

00:23:28.149 --> 00:23:29.580
doesn’t die.

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:36.559
And just when he seems doomed, he’s saved
by Laenor Velaryon, on his dragon Seasmoke.

00:23:36.559 --> 00:23:40.580
So they didn’t mention it til now, but Laenor
has a dragon.

00:23:40.580 --> 00:23:44.389
Because Laenor has Targaryen dragon blood,
through his mother Rhaenys Targaryen.

00:23:44.389 --> 00:23:50.529
Rhaenys Targaryen herself also has a dragon,
called Meleys, the Red Queen.

00:23:50.529 --> 00:23:55.190
The other dragonriders currently are Rhaenyra,
with the yellow dragon Syrax.

00:23:55.190 --> 00:23:56.970
And Daemon with the red dragon Caraxes.

00:23:56.970 --> 00:24:02.739
There are also a bunch of other dragons around
that currently don’t have riders – like

00:24:02.739 --> 00:24:08.260
Vermithor, the Bronze Fury, which was the
dragon of old King Jaehaerys.

00:24:08.260 --> 00:24:11.950
Silverwing was the dragon of Jaehaerys’
wife Alysanne.

00:24:11.950 --> 00:24:14.679
Dreamfyre was Rhaena Targaryen’s dragon.

00:24:14.679 --> 00:24:17.580
And old Vhagar is on the east coast somewhere.

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:21.450
Plus there are probably a bunch more hatchlings
and eggs on Dragonstone.

00:24:21.450 --> 00:24:25.600
We’ll see many more dragons later in the
story.

00:24:25.600 --> 00:24:28.779
Seasmoke is a silvery grey dragon.

00:24:28.779 --> 00:24:32.600
And he’s a young dragon, fast and nimble
in flight.

00:24:32.600 --> 00:24:38.139
He and Laenor burn the Triarchy from the sky,
while the Velaryons attack on the ground,

00:24:38.139 --> 00:24:40.960
led by Lord Corlys, and by Vaemond.

00:24:40.960 --> 00:24:46.149
Daemon goes after the Crabfeeder, and finally
kills the crab.

00:24:46.149 --> 00:24:51.769
In the book, Daemon cuts off the Crabfeeder’s
head, but in the show he butchers him off-screen.

00:24:51.769 --> 00:24:58.360
Daemon gets covered in the Crabfeeder’s
blood, which might be a bad idea.

00:24:58.360 --> 00:25:03.899
Cause according to behind-the-scenes info,
the Crabfeeder had greyscale, a disease that

00:25:03.899 --> 00:25:07.179
can be highly contagious.. and deadly.

00:25:07.179 --> 00:25:11.789
So is Daemon gonna get infected and turn into
a stone man?

00:25:11.789 --> 00:25:17.570
In the Game of Thrones show, greyscale can
be cured – Jorah Mormont and Shireen Baratheon

00:25:17.570 --> 00:25:20.059
are both cured of greyscale.

00:25:20.059 --> 00:25:21.950
In the books, it’s different.

00:25:21.950 --> 00:25:25.740
The books say there are different forms of
greyscale.

00:25:25.740 --> 00:25:28.200
The swift “grey plague” is deadly.

00:25:28.200 --> 00:25:32.989
But there’s a different form of the disease
that affects children, and it gives them stony

00:25:32.989 --> 00:25:37.450
grey skin but it doesn’t kill, and it’s
not contagious.

00:25:37.450 --> 00:25:43.190
So maybe Crabfeeder had a form of greyscale
that isn’t contagious, so Daemon is safe.

00:25:43.190 --> 00:25:49.029
There is also an idea in the books that Targaryens
are immune to diseases – that the blood

00:25:49.029 --> 00:25:54.570
of the dragon has “a purifying fire” that
saves Targaryens from getting sick.

00:25:54.570 --> 00:25:59.429
Daenerys Targaryen believes this, and she
never gets sick, even when she visits disease

00:25:59.429 --> 00:26:01.309
victims in the books.

00:26:01.309 --> 00:26:05.090
But some other Targaryens do die of disease.

00:26:05.090 --> 00:26:09.940
King Daeron Targaryen the Second and his grandkids
die of a plague.

00:26:09.940 --> 00:26:13.389
And Maegelle Targaryen dies of greyscale.

00:26:13.389 --> 00:26:18.399
So not all Targaryens are immune to disease,
but maybe some are.

00:26:18.399 --> 00:26:23.951
There are hints that it’s only Targaryens
who have dragons who don’t get sick – King

00:26:23.951 --> 00:26:26.690
Daeron and Maegelle don’t have dragons.

00:26:26.690 --> 00:26:28.749
But Daenerys and Daemon do have dragons.

00:26:28.749 --> 00:26:32.030
So maybe Daemon is immune.

00:26:32.030 --> 00:26:36.889
That said, Crabfeeder’s greyscale is not
in the books, it’s never actually mentioned

00:26:36.889 --> 00:26:41.919
in this show, and it sounds like the showrunners
just added it to make the Crabfeeder look

00:26:41.919 --> 00:26:42.989
scary.

00:26:42.989 --> 00:26:48.039
The point is, Daemon’s reckless violence
wins him victory.

00:26:48.039 --> 00:26:52.730
His blood-soaked killing is similar to Rhaenyra’s
violence with the boar.

00:26:52.730 --> 00:26:58.650
While King Viserys awkwardly slaughters a
defenceless deer, Rhaenyra and Daemon win

00:26:58.650 --> 00:27:01.779
real victories against real enemies.

00:27:01.779 --> 00:27:08.980
The showrunners say these characters are “reborn”,
finding new strength and purpose, forged stronger

00:27:08.980 --> 00:27:11.690
by fire and blood.

00:27:11.690 --> 00:27:16.869
If you want to know more about when the Lannisters
tried to get dragons from Rhaena Targaryen,

00:27:16.869 --> 00:27:23.509
or about King Jaehaerys’ rebellious daughters,
the full story is told in Fire &amp; Blood.

